From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 03:07:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 459/488] [DS4.1] The vision tower in TileLang

Under the TileLang backend the ViT and the aligner run TileLang kernels
only (B12X is not imported); the checkpoint's parameter tree is the same.
- Projections: BF16 GEMMs with the bias added in FP32 before the one
  rounding; gate/up and SwiGLU in one epilogue, bias and GELU in the
  aligner's first projection.
- RoPE in place in the qkv buffer; non-causal flash attention over one
  image reading q, k and v from it, columns past the live rows masked.
- Residual add fused with RMSNorm in B12X's reduction order; the spatial
  merge staged through shared memory; patch rows padded to whole tiles.
- Workspaces at the tower's capacity, allocated at binding; every kernel
  declared for preparation.
Gates: elementwise and rowwise ops bit for bit with B12X's arithmetic;
GEMMs and attention against FP64 within B12X's own error; the whole tower
and aligner against DeepSeek's math. benchmark_tilelang_vision.py --gate
times it against the B12X tower.
